i and Quin are on the same side.\\\\n\\\\nWait — let’s think carefully.\\\\n\\\\nLet’s suppose Dara is between Uma and Dmitri → Uma – Dara – Dmitri  \\\\nThen from clue 8: Dara is between Uma and Quin → Uma – Dara – Quin\\\\n\\\\nSo both Dmitri and Quin are on the same side of Dara? But that would mean Dara is between Uma and Quin, and also between Uma and Dmitri — so both Quin and Dmitri are on the same side of Dara.\\\\n\\\\nBut clue 8 says Dara is between Uma and Quin → so Uma and Quin are on opposite sides of Dara.\\\\n\\\\nSimilarly, clue 4: Dara is between Dmitri and Uma → Dmitri and Uma are on opposite sides of Dara.\\\\n\\\\nSo from clue 4: Dara is between Dmitri and Uma → so Dara is between them → so one of them is on left, one on right.\\\\n\\\\nFrom clue 8: Dara is between Uma and Quin → so Uma and Quin are on opposite sides of Dara.\\\\n\\\\nSo let’s suppose:\\\\n\\\\n- From clue 4: Dara is between Dmitri and Uma → so either:\\\\n  - Dmitri – Dara – Uma\\\\n  - or Uma – Dara – Dmitri\\\\n\\\\n- From clue 8: Dara is between Uma and Quin → so either:\\\\n  - Uma – Dara – Quin\\\\n  - or Quin – Dara – Uma\\\\n\\\\nNow, let’s try to combine.\\\\n\\\\nSuppose Dara is between Dmitri and Uma → Dmitri – Dara – Uma  \\\\nThen from clue 8: Dara is between Uma and Quin → so Uma and Quin must be on opposite sides of Dara → but Uma is on the right of Dara, so Quin must be on the left → Quin – Dara – Uma\\\\n\\\\nBut we already have Dmitri – Dara – Uma → so Quin and Dmitri are both on the left of Dara? That’s possible.\\\\n\\\\nSo we have: Quin – Dara – Uma, and also Dmitri – Dara – Uma → so both Quin and Dmitri are to the left of Dara, and Uma to the right.\\\\n\\\\nSo the order must be: Quin, Dmitri, Dara, Uma — but wait, Quin and Dmitri are both on the left — but we don’t know their order.\\\\n\\\\nBut Dara is between\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794482879,\\\