ign seats 1-7.\\\\n\\\\nLet's solve. Chain of 5: E(li) < J < B(o) < H < Be. Minimal positions 1,2,3,4,5 but Jun not seat2. Need include Zane and Elsa.\\\\n\\\\nElsa adjacent to Hana. Since Hana after Boris/Jun/Eli. Hana cannot seat1. Elsa can be Hana-1 or Hana+1. But if Elsa at Hana-1, then seat Hana-1 is occupied by Elsa, but Boris must be before Hana and not adjacent? Actually Boris and Elsa not neighboring. If Elsa immediately left of Hana, Boris could be elsewhere before Hana not adjacent to Elsa. If Elsa immediately right of Hana, then Ben must be after Hana; if Hana seat6 then no right? Need.\\\\n\\\\nLet's brute force mentally or systematic. Need any solution. Let's derive.\\\\n\\\\nLet positions:\\\\ne = Eli, j=Jun, b=Boris, h=Hana, n=Ben (use n), z=Zane, s=Elsa.\\\\n\\\\nConstraints:\\\\ne < j < b < h < n.\\\\ne < z < n.\\\\ns = h±1.\\\\ns != b±1.\\\\nj !=2.\\\\nAll distinct.\\\\n\\\\nNeed fill 7 seats.\\\\n\\\\nBecause chain length 5 plus z/s. Let's enumerate possible h maybe.\\\\n\\\\nSince e<j<b<h<n, h at most 6? Need Ben after Hana, so h<=6. Also b<h, j<b, e<j. Minimal before h: 3 seats plus h, so h>=4. Hana seat 4,5,6 maybe. If h=6 then Ben=7. Then e,j,b are 1,2,3? Since three before h and distinct increasing, must occupy seats 1,2,3. Jun not seat2, so Jun cannot be middle. Chain e<j<b in seats1,2,3. Possibilities: e=1,j=3,b=2? no b>j. e=1,j=2 invalid; e? only e=1,j=2,b=3 invalid. So h≠6? Wait if h=6, positions before h are exactly 1,2,3 for e,j,b. Jun not 2 impossible because e<j<b forces j=2. Yes h≠6.\\\\n\\\\nh=5: Then e,j,b occupy three of seats1-4 in increasing order, Ben >5 (6 or7). Zane between Eli and Ben, Elsa adjacent to Hana (4 or6), Boris/Elsa not adjacent. Need check.\\\\n\\\\nh=4: Then e,j,b occupy seats1-3 exactly (again j=2 invalid). So h≠4? Since three before h and h=4 => seats1,2,3; j=2 invalid. Thus h=5 only? Wait h=6 impossible, h=4 impossible. So Hana seat5. Nice.\\\\n\\\\nThen e<j<b<5, so e,j,b occupy three seats among 1,2,3,4 in increasing order. Jun not2. Ben >5: seat6 or7. Elsa adjacent to Hana seat5: Elsa seat4 or6. But Boris/Elsa not adjacent. If Elsa seat4, Boris must not seat3 or5; Boris<5 and not seat? Could be seat1? But if Boris seat1 then Jun before Boris impossible. Boris seat2? Jun before, possible? e<j<2\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794482880,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":207,\\\"total_tokens\\\":1207,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":1000,\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\":null,\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":0,\\\"completion_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":0}}}\",\"signature\":{\"text\":\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:277f99388f525a5a399422b88c9d2e1e2eb9fd7adc10e874f68b38555ac652e0:9a35037c9d6781ff22bb8d468e0b78899fdcbf4e2c9a8d75f647a98b795dfe19\",\"signature\":\"0x06c24689c7cbea2ad38d6166f24b16031a4bf0193fbb85f6418f9b9ea52ab363522e856d31f2892b4ac3c8c3926fa2822a8db400f7336e078f4eb4e84f40b1951c\",\"signing_address\":\"0x3b753b4406613c5e70ae640508632b600424fa0c\",\"signing_algo\":\"ecdsa\",\"signature_kind\":\"provider_tee\"},\"verdict\":{\"ok\":false,\"reason\":\"no <answer> block\"}},{\"task\":4,\"model\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct\",\"response\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-a186f063-85fe-4c3c-b983-a7dbc39b1a43\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"chat.completion\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"We are given a logic puzzle involving six people: **Elsa, Uma, Iris, Lena, Xena, Wade**, sitting in a row of six seats numbered 1 to 6 from left to right.\\\\n\\\\nWe need to determine the order of the people from seat 1 to seat 6, satisfying all the conditions.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### **Given Conditions:**\\\\n\\\\n1. **Elsa sat somewhere between Uma and Iris.**  \\\\n   → So, Uma and Iris are on opposite sides of Elsa. That is, the order is either:  \\\\n   - Uma, Elsa, Iris  \\\\n   - Iris, Elsa, Uma  \\\\n   (Elsa is between them, not necessarily adjacent)\\\\n\\\\n2. **Lena sat in the first or the last seat.**  \\\\n   → Lena is in seat 1 or seat 6.\\\\n\\\\n3. **Iris sat somewhere to the left of Xena.**  \\\\n   → Iris < Xena (in seat number)\\\\n\\\\n4. **Xena and Wade sat in neighbouring seats.**  \\\\n   → |Xena - Wade| = 1\\\\n\\\\n5. **Uma sat somewhere between Wade and Iris.**  \\\\n   → So, Wade and Iris are on opposite sides of Uma.  \\\\n   → Order: Wade, Uma, Iris or Iris, Uma, Wade\\\\n\\\\n6. **Xena sat in the first or the last seat.**  \\\\n   → Xena is in seat 1 or seat 6.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nLet’s analyze step by step.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 1: Use conditions 2 and 6\\\\n\\\\n- **Lena** is in seat 1 or 6  \\\\n- **Xena** is in seat 1 or 6\\\\n\\\\nSo both Lena and Xena are in the end seats (1 or 6). Since there are only two end seats, and two people (Lena and Xena) who must be in end seats, **Lena and Xena are in seats 1 and 6**, in some order.\\\\n\\\\nSo:\\\\n- {Lena, Xena} = {1, 6}\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 2: Use condition 3: Iris is to the left of Xena\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris < Xena\\\\n\\\\nBut Xena is in seat 1 or 6.\\\\n\\\\n- If Xena is in seat 1 → Iris < 1 → impossible (no seat 0)\\\\n- So Xena **cannot** be in seat 1\\\\n\\\\nTherefore, **Xena must be in seat 6**\\\\n\\\\nThen, from condition 6: Xena is in 1 or 6 → so Xena = 6\\\\n\\\\nThen, from condition 2: Lena is in 1 or 6 → but 6 is taken by Xena → so **Lena = 1**\\\\n\\\\nSo far:\\\\n- Seat 1: Lena\\\\n- Seat 6: Xena\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 3: Xena and Wade are in neighboring seats\\\\n\\\\nXena is in seat 6 → so Wade must be in seat 5 (only neighbor)\\\\n\\\\nSo **Wade = 5**\\\\n\\\\nNow we have:\\\\n- 1: Lena\\\\n- 5: Wade\\\\n- 6: Xena\\\\n\\\\nRemaining seats: 2, 3, 4  \\\\nRemaining people: Elsa, Uma, Iris\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 4: Iris is to the left of Xena\\\\n\\\\nXena is in 6 → Iris < 6 → so Iris is in 2, 3, or 4 → OK\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 5: Uma sat somewhere between Wade and Iris\\\\n\\\\nWade is in 5\\\\n\\\\nSo Uma is between Wade and Iris → so either:\\\\n- Wade, Uma, Iris → but Wade is in 5 → so Uma would be in 6, Iris in 7 → impossible\\\\n- Or Iris, Uma, Wade → so Iris < Uma < Wade = 5\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris < Uma < 5\\\\n\\\\nSo Uma must be in 2, 3, or 4, but less than 5 → OK\\\\n\\\\nAnd Iris < Uma\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris < Uma < 5\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris and Uma are in seats 2, 3, 4, with Iris < Uma\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 6: Elsa sat somewhere between Uma and Iris\\\\n\\\\nSo Elsa is between Uma and Iris → so either:\\\\n- Uma, Elsa, Iris → then Uma < Elsa < Iris\\\\n- Or Iris, Elsa, Uma → then Iris < Elsa < Uma\\\\n\\\\nBut from above, we have **Iris < Uma** (from Uma between Wade and Iris → Iris < Uma < 5)\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris < Uma\\\\n\\\\nSo the only possibility for Elsa to be between them is:\\\\n- Iris, Elsa, Uma → so Iris < Elsa < Uma\\\\n\\\\nSo we have:\\\\n- Iris < Elsa < Uma < 5\\\\n\\\\nAnd all three (Iris, Elsa, Uma) are in seats 2,\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794482879,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":181,\\\"total_tokens\\\":1181,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":1000}}\",\"signature\":{\"text\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct:0ea1240578740b4d7c1f43531b3f02257b57856993e9088aaeaaf85bdc932e8e:8053e3e014113a5585a78fee8aed33318a0fae494836e9ed3b969dbcb52e71b6\",\"signature\":\"0x99f452618d64612226b67e619b14225ff8e4493f5c00f332118a9d25db7cff606bb176f541df812ee9b096324bc1879d4b835011f79648f8311b78c74550409e1c\",\"signing_address\":\"0x2665cce942fa427ef30d87f4b0bff67fb7645462\",\"signing_algo\":\"ecdsa\",\"signature_kind\":\"provider_tee\"},\"verdict\":{\"ok\":false,\"reason\":\"no <answer> block\"}},{\"task\":4,\"model\":\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\",\"response\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"b9ba6d901b4741f88352c4cae904a108\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"chat.completion\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"<answer>Lena, Iris, Elsa, Uma, Wade, Xena</answer>\\\",\\\"reasoning_content\\\":\\\"We need solve logic puzzle. Need provide order. Let's parse.\\\\n\\\\nPeople: Elsa E, Uma U, Iris I, Lena L, Xena X, Wade W. Seats 1-6 left to right.\\\\n\\\\nConditions:\\\\n1 Elsa sat somewhere between Uma and Iris. Means seat(E) strictly between seat(U) and seat(I). Could U<E<I or I<E<U.\\\\n2 Lena sat in first or last seat: L seat 1 or 6.\\\\n3 Iris sat somewhere to left of Xena: I < X.\\\\n4 Xena and Wade sat in neighbouring seats: |X-W|=1.\\\\n5 Uma sat somewhere between Wade and Iris: U strictly between W and I. Could W<U<I or I<U<W.\\\\n6 Xena sat in first or last seat: X seat 1 or 6.\\\\n\\\\nNeed find all? Need any. Let's solve carefully. Since X first or last and Iris left of Xena. If X=1, no seat left of X for Iris, impossible. So X=6. Then Iris <6. Wade neighbor of X => W=5. Lena seat 1 or 6; X=6 so Lena=1. Uma between Wade(5) and Iris. Since W=5, I<5 and U between I and 5: I < U < 5. Also Iris left of Xena satisfied. Elsa between Uma and Iris: E between U and I. Since I<U<5, E also between I and U, so I < E < U <5. Remaining seats: 1 Lena, 5 Wade, 6 Xena. Seats 2,3,4 for Iris,Elsa,Uma with I<E<U. Thus I=2,E=3,U=4. Unique. Answer: Lena, Iris, Elsa, Uma, Wade, Xena.\\\\n\\\\nNeed final with answer tags. Ensure comma-separated names.\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"stop\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null,\\\"matched_stop\\\":154827}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794482879,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":185,\\\"total_tokens\\\":593,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":408,\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"cached_tokens\\\":0},\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":389,\\\"completion_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":389}}}\",\"signature\":{\"text\":\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:d6f6410111f36e4c88af569d563b0029dce5d36c3bd087fc09b4c73bd626dd7c:6460411cc08fe5864ba83cf6ae3bcebe826598259d6c8eedb46358cd96412301\",\"signature\":\"0xb47fabbaf514abb5862d